One little caveat; otherwise you've got it:

A sacrifice bunt can advance any runner on any base any number of bases, although it's extremely rare that it's more than one (usually the subsequent advancement is on an error).  But a sacrifice fly is only credited if a runner scores.  A fly ball that advances a runner from first to second or from second to third is just scored as a fly out.

